A||||12||Alex2004||Why doesn't the Radiator fan ever come on?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||12-30-2000||05:50 PM||||I have never seen the fan come on, the car has been up to 220 before and it never kicked on. What do you think is wrong, we've had it for over a year now, and have never seen it on. Any ideas? Thanks<BR>Alex...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||12-30-2000||06:07 PM||||It will...fan dosnt kick on until it hits 235 I believe..let it sit running idle in your driveway on a warm/hot day and let it hit 235, itll come on.....(wait until the weather is right, you can forget it reaching that temp in cold weather).<BR>I thought the same thing about mine until I finally just let it run for a while (like mentioned above)..it finally came on.<BR>If your gauge starts hitting the red area and it dosnt come on, then thats another story...but Im sure it works fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||12-30-2000||07:34 PM||||Ok, that's good to hear! Thanks<BR>Alex...<P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||2xsess||12-30-2000||08:16 PM||||A quick way to make sure that the fan works at all is to turn on the A/C, it will come on as soon as you turn on the A/C. <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||12-30-2000||08:35 PM||||It doesn't work then either!!!! Man, that's odd... What do you think it is if it doesn't come on with the a/c? Let me know. Thanks<BR>Alex...<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:Alex917@excite.com">Alex917@excite.com</A> ||||reg||11
Z||000005||rodmcneill||12-30-2000||08:54 PM||||There is a fan relay that goes bad. I replaced mine recently. It is near the drivers side headlight. I would suggest getting a Delco original part, the generic one I installed a year ago was inferior construction.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rodmcneill||12-30-2000||09:15 PM||||There is something I forgot to mention. Check with test light that there is power going into the relay and you can also jumper the relay to the fan motor to see if it turns. You could possibly have a bad fan motor but chances are it is the relay.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Notchit||12-31-2000||04:20 AM||||Yeah i was worried too at first, i mean you start up a car, drive it for a while and the fan didn't go on....in fact i still haven't seen it go on, but i haven't used my car yet. I turned on the A/C and i heard that whirr...opened up the front hood and it was working fine, so i am not worried about that anymore, try doing the same just turn on your A/C. that way you know for a fact the motor isn't busted   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000008||Notchit||12-31-2000||04:21 AM||||k, basicly do what Jeff told you to do....i'm a moron and didn't read it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000009||rogergarrison||12-31-2000||11:37 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>There is a fan relay that goes bad. I replaced mine recently. It is near the drivers side headlight. I would suggest getting a Delco original part, the generic one I installed a year ago was inferior construction.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey it sure pays to read these posts even if your not having a problem. I just noticed rods mention of a relay for fan in drivers side front cmpt. Id disconnected all of the relays under there when i did my custom headlites. I thought they were all related to headlite motors. I opened it up and sure enough my fan was not working. plugged the connector back in and yahoo, fan came on. Thanks bud, I would never have noticed it in ohio during this cold, but id have been lost with a breakdown this summer and no idea why.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||14
